# Gokez-Mart — Project Rules for Cline

## Speed Protocol (follow strictly)
- Respond fast: keep explanations short. Default to "change + 1-line summary". Give long explanations only if asked.
- Batch all independent tool calls (reads, searches, edits) into one response.
- Prefer narrow edits over broad rewrites; do not restructure code the user didn't ask for.
- Never read package.json / config files you don't need — commands and stack are documented below.
- If the user names a file, read only that file first; avoid repo-wide exploration.
- Verify with the smallest possible test/lint command (targeted file, not full suite).
- Do not run builds or full test suites unless explicitly asked or a change is large/cross-cutting.
- No placeholder code: always complete, working code.

## Repo Map (monorepo, npm workspaces)
Root: /Volumes/Entertainment/VS_code/My_working_projects/gokez-mart
Node: 20.x (see .nvmrc). Root package.json only has dev:* convenience scripts.

- `mart-backend/` — Express API. CommonJS, TypeScript, tsx dev runner.
  - `src/`: index.ts, app.ts, config, controllers, routes, services, middleware, utils, database, types
  - Tests in `tests/*.test.ts`
- `mart-user/` — Vite + React 18 customer web app (port 5177), Tailwind, zustand, axios.
  - `src/`: pages, components, hooks, store, services, constants, utils
  - Tests in `tests/*.test.ts`
- `mart-hub/` — Vite + React admin panel (port 5178), Tailwind, zustand, axios, react-hook-form.
  - `src/`: pages, components, hooks, store, services, utils
- `mart-mobile/` — mobile app
- `docs/` — audit/implementation docs; `FEATURES.txt` — feature list; `README.md` — project overview
- Deploy: Railway (`railway.json`), Render (`render.yaml`), Docker (`docker-compose.local.yml`)

## Exact Commands (do not re-discover)
All run from repo root (npm workspaces):
- Backend:   `npm run dev:api`        (tsx watch)
- Web:       `npm run dev:web`        (vite, port 5177)
- Admin:     `npm run dev:admin`      (vite, port 5178)
- Backend build: `npm run build --workspace=mart-backend`
- Backend test:  `npm run test --workspace=mart-backend`          (node --test, all)
- Web test:      `npm run test --workspace=mart-user`
- Targeted test (fastest): `node --import tsx --test <workspace>/tests/<file>.test.ts`
- DB migrate:    `npm run db:migrate --workspace=mart-backend`
- Web build:     `npm run build --workspace=mart-user`
- Admin build:   `npm run build --workspace=mart-hub`

## Conventions
- TypeScript everywhere; keep existing patterns/style of the touched file.
- Backend: pg (Postgres), express-validator, helmet/hpp security middleware, OpenTelemetry + Sentry already wired.
- Frontend: react-router-dom v6, zustand for state, axios for API, Tailwind CSS, lucide-react icons.
- Keep changes minimal and scoped to the task; do not rename or move files unless asked.
